    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51234" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστάνω</span></b> , later collat. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵστημι</span>, first in inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστάνειν, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			<u>PPetr.</u>
			2p.120
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			<u>Michel</u>
			1006.22
		</span></i> (Teos, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συν-</span>)
			<i><span class="en">
			Plb.
			3.108.4
		</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαθ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Ascl.
			<u>Tact.</u>
			10.9
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			Dsc.
			4.43
		</span></i>, etc.; cf. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστάναι Ἀττικοί, ἱστάνειν Ἕλληνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Moer.
					200
				</span></i>
			; part. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιστάνοντες</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				11.2.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἱστάνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simp.
					<u>in Ph.</u>
					1257.34
				</span></i>
			: ind. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστάνει</span> Philistio
				ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.115e
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστάνομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
					3.31
				</span></i>
			, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιστάνουσι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.266S.
			</span></i>, etc.: impf. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συν</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίστανον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.5.6
			</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hisp.</u>
				36
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστανόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1343.26
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>:—introduced by the copyists into
				<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				25.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				2.29
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
